{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"33ae652f9199f0781d5d5e5df912695ef1f31e85"},"timestamp":1509481049,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNzAxMDQ2NjM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1948","origin":"github"},"title":"Automagic - Path as binary object - pandas","message":"#### What is the problem?\nOpening files with pandas using AutomagicIO fails. This is because pandas (perhaps due to to using CPython?) returns a bytes object for the file name, so statements such as `'annex/objects' in realpath(filepath)` will return an error, because filepath is not a string.\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\nOpen a file that Datalad would have to fetch using `pandas.read_csv`\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using?\nLatest version of Datalad on Ubuntu in Docker.","files":null}]}